Cluster lift

The default landscape layout puts the left and right clusters (shoulder
buttons, stick, D-pad / ABXY) at the bottom corners, where a game draws
its own HUD (health bars, minimap). The layout editor moves single
buttons and sticks, but an app cannot change the default positions.

New optional ControllerView init parameter clusterLift: points the left
and the right cluster are raised in the landscape layout (an offset: the
centre buttons stay where they are). Default (0, 0): unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted.

